{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כנוח", :translit "k'nuach", :gloss "as resting"} {:he "ויהי כנוח עליהם הרוח", :translit "vayehi k'nuach aleihem ha-ruach", :gloss "and it came to pass as resting upon them the spirit"} {:he "כנוח כפות רגלי הכהנים", :translit "k'nuach kapot raglei ha-kohanim", :gloss "as resting soles of feet of the priests"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויהי כנוח עליהם הרוח" "כנוח כפות רגלי הכהנים"]}], :frame {:text "In 1 Kings 8:8 the verse states that the poles of the Ark could be seen as 'resting' (כנוח) against the curtain from the Holy. The phrase 'כנוח כפות רגלי הכהנים' in Joshua 3:13 describes the moment the priests' feet 'rested' at the Jordan's edge, after which the Ark stood and the waters were cut off (Joshua 3:13, 3:16). Ba'al HaTurim links these to show that the Spirit's 'resting' (Numbers 11:25) mirrors the presence of the Shechinah that abode between the cherubim atop the Ark (Exodus 25:22).", :sources ["1 Kings 8:8" "Joshua 3:13" "Joshua 3:16" "Numbers 11:25" "Exodus 25:22"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויהי כנוח עליהם הרוח" "כנוח כפות רגלי הכהנים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ויהי כנוח עליהם הרוח", :refs ["Numbers 11:25"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כנוח כפות רגלי הכהנים", :refs ["Joshua 3:13"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:28:27.145070684Z", :model "glm-5.2"}